IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Radio-communication Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 3), 1999 Revised Edition (1 July 1999), made under section 131 of the Telecommunication Authority of Singapore Act (Cap. 323), the "repealed Act" of the Telecommunications Act 1999.
-- Text: TA1999-RADIO99 under subjects/sg/telecommunications-radio-communication-regulations-1999/registers/source-bundle/ (the e-Gazette's copy, deposited 2026-11-04 from the follow-up list; sha256 in the .meta.json).
-- The title page prints "Rg 3, 1995 Ed., G.N. No. S 328/94, Amended by S 144/96, S 161/97, S 615/98, S 227/99, REVISED EDITION 1999 (1.7.1999)".  None of those instruments is deposited; the Revised Edition incorporates them.
-- NAME COLLISION.  This is "Cap. 323, Rg 3" in the 1999 Edition.  The encoding's "Rg 3" elsewhere (sgta-i-rg3-*.l4) is the Class Licences Regulations of the 2002 Revised Edition.  Here the 1999 text is always called "Rg 3 (1999 Ed.)".
--
-- WHEN IT APPLIES.  The Telecommunications Act 1999 came into operation on 1 December 1999 (s 3(1)); s 98(2) continues subsidiary legislation "made under the repealed Act ... and in force immediately before 1 December 1999 ... as if made under this Act
-- until it is revoked or repealed by subsidiary legislation made under this Act" (TA1999.txt:7097-7102).  So this text answers from 1 December 1999.
-- It ended on 1 March 2001, the day before the Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations 2001 (S 114/2001) came into operation on 2 March 2001: reg 80(1) of S 114/2001 reads "The Radio-communication Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 3) are revoked."
-- (TA1999-RG5-S114-2001.txt:1548-1549; encoded in sgta-i-rg5-as-made.l4; that Rg 5 version table already answers NOTHING before 2 March 2001, so the two tables tile).
-- Amendments between 1 July 1999 and 1 March 2001 are not known to this encoding (none is deposited; the Revised Edition is the latest text held).  A date before 1 December 1999 answers NOTHING (the TAS Act period is outside the scope of the Telecommunications Act encoding).
--
-- WHAT IT DOES.  A "station" is "a transmitter, receiver, a combination of transmitters and receivers or any accessory thereto which is used or intended to be used for radio-communication" (reg 2).  Reg 4(1): "Except as provided in the First Schedule,
-- no person shall possess, establish, install or use any station in any place or on board any local vessel or aircraft or in any vehicle in Singapore unless he has a valid licence granted under these Regulations."  The First Schedule lists the equipment "for which no station licence is
-- required for in-building or localised on-site operations" (15 items, with item 11(e) "TV Receivers/ Radio Systems" among remote control devices, item 14 "Stand-alone GPS Receivers" and item 15 "Communication Receivers (excluding scanning devices) and Microwave Multipoint
-- Distribution Systems (MMDS) Receivers"); Part IIIA (reg 53A) deems a class licence to a person who possesses or uses a "relevant radio-communication station" (one connected with a public cellular, paging, data, trunked radio or satellite mobile system, or capable of being so used).
-- Reg 57 makes a contravention of any provision an offence.  This module quotes and encodes the text; whether any of it reaches a particular receiver is a question for the seat modules and TV-QUESTION.md, not for this layer.

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:159 | Citation
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:160 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:161 | Regulations.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 1 (citation) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:159-161)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date, as continued by s 98(2) (from 1 December 1999 until revoked by reg 80(1) of S 114/2001, in operation 2 March 2001)` MEANS
    d AT LEAST (Date 1 12 1999) AND d LESS THAN (Date 2 3 2001)

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:163 | Definitions
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:164 | 2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:165 | ‘‘Amateur Station’’ means a station in respect of which an
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:166 | Amateur Station licensee is authorised in the licence to use;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:167 | ‘‘armed forces’’ means the Singapore Armed Forces established
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:168 | under the Singapore Armed Forces Act (Cap. 295) and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:169 | includes any visiting force, not being a police force, which is
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:170 | lawfully present in Singapore;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:171 | ‘‘Armed Forces Communication’’ means radio-communication —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:172 | (a) between stations of the armed forces; or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:173 | (b) between stations of the armed forces and any other
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:174 | radio-communication station, whether on shore or on
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:175 | any vessel or aircraft;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:176 | ‘‘authorised officer’’ means any person authorised by the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:177 | Authority to act on its behalf;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:178 | ‘‘class licence’’ means a class licence granted under regulation
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:179 | 53A;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:180 | ‘‘class licensee’’ means a person who is deemed to have been
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:181 | granted a class licence;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:182 | ‘‘International Telecommunication Convention’’ means the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:183 | Convention of the International Telecommunication Union
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:184 | signed at Nairobi in 1982 or any subsequent revision or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:185 | modification thereof to which the Government of Singapore
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:186 | is a party;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:188 | ‘‘licence’’ means any licence granted under these Regulations in
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:189 | respect of any station or network, but does not, except in
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:190 | relation to regulations 3, 4 (1), (2) and (6), 6, 14, 16, 19, 21
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:191 | and 60, include a class licence;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:192 | ‘‘licensee’’ means any person to whom a licence has been granted
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:193 | under these Regulations, and includes his employees, but
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:194 | does not, except in relation to regulations 6, 14 and 19,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:195 | include a class licensee;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:196 | ‘‘localised private network’’ means a private network that
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:197 | provides radio coverage of a confined or restricted area as
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:198 | specified by the Authority and that comprises at least 2
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:199 | stations each operating generally at an effective radiated
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:200 | power of 5 watts or below;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:201 | ‘‘Localised Radio-communication Station’’ means a station
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:202 | which can only be used for communication with a base
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:203 | station or with another station within a defined power limit
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:204 | specified by the Authority;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:205 | ‘‘network’’ means 2 or more stations operated by a person and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:206 | used or intended to be used in communication with one
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:207 | another;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:208 | ‘‘private network’’ means a network which exists to meet the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:209 | exclusive internal telecommunication needs of the licensee or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:210 | which has a number of common interest groups of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:211 | subscribers or users and radio channels as the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:212 | specify;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:213 | ‘‘public mobile network’’ means any public network that enables
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:214 | radio-communications through the use of portable or mobile
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:215 | stations and may include any of the following telecommuni-
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:216 | cation systems licensed under section 26 of the Act:
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:217 | (a) a public cellular mobile telephone system;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:218 | (b) a public radio paging system;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:219 | (c) a public data system; or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:220 | (d) a public trunked radio system;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:221 | ‘‘public network’’ means a network which is accessible to any
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:222 | member of the public generally and which is used or intended
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:223 | to be used to provide telecommunication services by means
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:224 | of radio-communication to the general public;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:227 | ‘‘Radio Regulations’’ means the Radio Regulations annexed to
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:228 | the International Telecommunication Convention and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:229 | includes every revision or modification thereof which the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:230 | Government has ratified or accepted;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:231 | ‘‘station’’ means a transmitter, receiver, a combination of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:232 | transmitters and receivers or any accessory thereto which is
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:233 | used or intended to be used for radio-communication;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:234 | ‘‘wide-area private network’’ means a private network that
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:235 | provides radio coverage of a wide area as specified by the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:236 | Authority and that comprises one or more stations operating
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:237 | generally at an effective radiated power of more than 5 watts.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:240 | PART II
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:241 | GENERAL LICENSING CONDITIONS
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 2 (definitions) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:163-241)
GIVEN `the thing is a transmitter, a receiver, a combination of transmitters and receivers, or any accessory to them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used or intended to be used for radio-communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 2: the thing is a "station"` MEANS
    `the thing is a transmitter, a receiver, a combination of transmitters and receivers, or any accessory to them` AND `it is used or intended to be used for radio-communication`

GIVEN `the network is of 2 or more stations operated by a person and used or intended to be used in communication with one another` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 2: the stations form a "network"` MEANS `the network is of 2 or more stations operated by a person and used or intended to be used in communication with one another`

GIVEN `the station is connected with a public cellular mobile telephone system, a public radio paging system, a public data system, a public trunked radio system or a public satellite mobile telephone or data system licensed under section 26 of the Act, or is capable of being used in connection with one but is not in use and not so connected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 53A(4): the station is a "relevant radio-communication station"` MEANS `the station is connected with a public cellular mobile telephone system, a public radio paging system, a public data system, a public trunked radio system or a public satellite mobile telephone or data system licensed under section 26 of the Act, or is capable of being used in connection with one but is not in use and not so connected`

GIVEN `the person holds a licence granted under the Regulations in respect of a station or network` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 2: the person is a "licensee"` MEANS `the person holds a licence granted under the Regulations in respect of a station or network`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:243 | Licensing authority
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:244 | 3. The licensing authority in respect of every licence granted under
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:245 | these Regulations shall be the Authority acting with the consent of, or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:246 | under the terms of a general authority given by, the Minister.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 3 (licensing authority) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:243-246)
GIVEN `the Authority acts with the consent of, or under the terms of a general authority given by, the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 3: the Authority is the licensing authority for the licence` MEANS `the Authority acts with the consent of, or under the terms of a general authority given by, the Minister`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:248 | Licence required before establishment of station or network
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:249 | 4.—(1) Except as provided in the First Schedule, no person shall
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:250 | possess, establish, install or use any station in any place or on board
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:251 | any local vessel or aircraft or in any vehicle in Singapore unless he has
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:252 | a valid licence granted under these Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:253 | (2) Notwithstanding the grant of any licence under these
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:254 | Regulations in respect of any station, no person shall establish or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:255 | operate any network in Singapore unless he has a valid network
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:256 | licence granted under these Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:257 | (3) Every application for a licence shall be made in such form and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:258 | manner which the Authority may, from time to time, determine for
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:259 | each class of licence and shall be supported by such information as the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:260 | Authority may require.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:261 | (4) The Authority may require any application for any licence to
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:262 | be submitted, instead of to the Authority, to any operator of a
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:263 | telecommunication system or service authorised by the Authority to
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:265 | receive and process applications for licences on the Authority’s
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:266 | behalf.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:267 | (5) A licensee shall notify the Authority of any change in his
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:268 | personal particulars specified in a licence within 14 days of such
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:269 | change.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:270 | (6) A licence granted under these Regulations shall be valid for
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:271 | such period as the Authority may determine unless revoked or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:272 | suspended in accordance with the provisions of the Act or these
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:273 | Regulations, and shall be subject to such conditions, restrictions and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:274 | limitations as the Authority may, from time to time, determine.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:275 | (7) The Authority may at any time vary all or any of the conditions
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:276 | upon which a licence is granted or impose additional conditions and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:277 | a licensee shall, at his own expense, comply with the varied or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:278 | additional conditions.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 4 (licence required before establishment of station or network) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:248-278)
GIVEN `the person possesses, establishes, installs or uses the station` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is any place, or on board a local vessel or aircraft, or in a vehicle, in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the station is provided for by the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a valid licence granted under the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(1): the person contravenes the regulation` MEANS
        `the person possesses, establishes, installs or uses the station`
    AND `the place is any place, or on board a local vessel or aircraft, or in a vehicle, in Singapore`
    AND (NOT `the station is provided for by the First Schedule`)
    AND (NOT `the person has a valid licence granted under the Regulations`)

GIVEN `the person establishes or operates the network in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a valid network licence granted under the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(2): the person contravenes the regulation, despite the grant of a licence in respect of any station` MEANS
    `the person establishes or operates the network in Singapore` AND (NOT `the person has a valid network licence granted under the Regulations`)

GIVEN `the application is in the form and manner the Authority determines for each class of licence and supported by the information it requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(3): the application is in order` MEANS `the application is in the form and manner the Authority determines for each class of licence and supported by the information it requires`

GIVEN `the Authority requires the application to be submitted to an operator of a telecommunication system or service authorised to receive and process applications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(4): the application is to be submitted to the operator instead of to the Authority` MEANS `the Authority requires the application to be submitted to an operator of a telecommunication system or service authorised to receive and process applications`

GIVEN `days after the change in personal particulars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(5): the licensee has notified the Authority within the time` MEANS `days after the change in personal particulars` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `the licence has been revoked or suspended in accordance with the Act or the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(6): the licence remains valid for the period the Authority determined` MEANS NOT `the licence has been revoked or suspended in accordance with the Act or the Regulations`

GIVEN `the Authority has varied the conditions or imposed additional conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee complies with them at its own expense` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(7): the licensee is meeting the varied or additional conditions` MEANS
    (NOT `the Authority has varied the conditions or imposed additional conditions`) OR `the licensee complies with them at its own expense`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:280 | No assignment, transfer, etc., of benefits of licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:281 | 5.—(1) Except with the consent in writing of the Authority, a
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:282 | licensee shall not assign, transfer, sublet or otherwise dispose of the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:283 | benefit of any licence granted under these Regulations, or permit
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:284 | another person to participate in any of the benefits, powers or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:285 | authority granted under such licence.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:286 | (2) Except with the consent in writing of the Authority, every
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:287 | licensed station and network shall be under the control of the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:288 | licensee.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 5 (no assignment, transfer, etc., of benefits of licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:280-288)
GIVEN `the licensee assigns, transfers, sublets or otherwise disposes of the benefit of the licence, or permits another person to participate in its benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 5(1): the licensee contravenes the regulation` MEANS
    `the licensee assigns, transfers, sublets or otherwise disposes of the benefit of the licence, or permits another person to participate in its benefits` AND (NOT `the Authority consented in writing`)

GIVEN `the licensed station or network is under the control of the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority consented in writing to another arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 5(2): the licensee is meeting the regulation` MEANS `the licensed station or network is under the control of the licensee` OR `the Authority consented in writing to another arrangement`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:290 | Employees of licensee
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:291 | 6. The licensee shall ensure that his employees comply with the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:292 | provisions of the Act, these Regulations and the conditions of the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:293 | licence.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 6 (employees of licensee) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:290-293)
GIVEN `the licensee ensures that its employees comply with the Act, the Regulations and the conditions of the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 6: the licensee is meeting the regulation` MEANS `the licensee ensures that its employees comply with the Act, the Regulations and the conditions of the licence`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:295 | Equipment in stations or networks
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:296 | 7.—(1) The Authority may, in respect of any individual or class of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:297 | station or network licence, specify the type of equipment that the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:298 | licensee is authorised to use and, if applicable, the type of equipment
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:299 | to be comprised in the individual or class of station or network.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:300 | (2) A licensed station or network shall not be changed or modified
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:301 | in respect of any of the particulars mentioned in the licence, including
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:302 | the equipment comprised therein, the operating frequencies and the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:305 | location at which the station or network is installed, except with the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:306 | prior approval of the Authority.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 7 (equipment in stations or networks) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:295-306)
GIVEN `the Authority has specified the type of equipment the licensee is authorised to use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is of the specified type` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 7(1): the licensee is authorised to use the equipment` MEANS
    (NOT `the Authority has specified the type of equipment the licensee is authorised to use`) OR `the equipment is of the specified type`

GIVEN `the licensed station or network is changed or modified in a particular mentioned in the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority gave its prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 7(2): the licensee contravenes the regulation` MEANS
    `the licensed station or network is changed or modified in a particular mentioned in the licence` AND (NOT `the Authority gave its prior approval`)

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:308 | Records
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:309 | 7A.—(1) A licensee of a network shall keep an up-to-date record
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:310 | of the radio-communication equipment comprised in the network.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:311 | (2) The record shall —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:312 | (a) contain such information;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:313 | (b) be kept in such form; and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:314 | (c) be submitted to the Authority at such intervals,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:315 | as the Authority may, from time to time, require.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:316 | (3) The licensee shall, at all reasonable times, permit an authorised
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:317 | officer to inspect and make copies of any entry in the record.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 7A (records) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:308-317)
GIVEN `the licensee of a network keeps an up-to-date record of the radio-communication equipment comprised in the network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record contains the information, is kept in the form and is submitted at the intervals the Authority requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee permits an authorised officer at all reasonable times to inspect and make copies of any entry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 7A: the licensee of a network is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    `the licensee of a network keeps an up-to-date record of the radio-communication equipment comprised in the network`
    AND `the record contains the information, is kept in the form and is submitted at the intervals the Authority requires`
    AND `the licensee permits an authorised officer at all reasonable times to inspect and make copies of any entry`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:319 | Restriction on grant of licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:320 | 8. A licence shall only be granted by the Authority, in its
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:321 | discretion, to —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:322 | (a) a person who is a citizen of Singapore;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:323 | (b) a company incorporated under the Companies Act
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:324 | (Cap. 50);
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:325 | (c) a business registered under the Business Registration Act
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:326 | (Cap. 32); or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:327 | (d) such other person as the Authority may, in its discretion,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:328 | think fit.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 8 (restriction on grant of licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:319-328)
GIVEN `the person is a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a company incorporated under the Companies Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a business registered under the Business Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority in its discretion thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 8: the Authority may grant a licence to the person` MEANS
    `the person is a citizen of Singapore` OR `the person is a company incorporated under the Companies Act` OR `the person is a business registered under the Business Registration Act` OR `the Authority in its discretion thinks fit`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:330 | Replacement licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:331 | 9.—(1) If the Authority is satisfied that any licence issued by it has
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:332 | been lost, destroyed or defaced, the Authority may, upon payment of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:333 | a fee of $5, issue a replacement licence.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:334 | (2) No replacement licence shall be issued in place of a defaced
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:335 | licence unless the defaced licence is surrendered to the Authority for
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:336 | cancellation.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 9 (replacement licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:330-336)
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied that the licence has been lost, destroyed or defaced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee of $5 has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence is defaced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defaced licence is surrendered to the Authority for cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 9: the Authority may issue a replacement licence` MEANS
        `the Authority is satisfied that the licence has been lost, destroyed or defaced`
    AND `the fee of $5 has been paid`
    AND ((NOT `the licence is defaced`) OR `the defaced licence is surrendered to the Authority for cancellation`)

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:338 | Amendment of licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:339 | 10.—(1) Amendments to a licence for the transfer of location of a
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:340 | station other than a portable or mobile station from one site to
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:341 | another or any change in the radio-communication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:343 | comprised in the station may only be made if the station has been
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:344 | satisfactorily inspected by an authorised officer and the Authority has
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:345 | approved the transfer or change.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:346 | (2) Where an authorised officer inspects a station or network
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:347 | under paragraph (1), the Authority may impose a fee of $70 for the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:348 | inspection.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:349 | (3) Any amendment to a licence for a change in the base or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:350 | repeater station in the network may only be made if —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:351 | (a) the licensee has notified the Authority of the change;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:352 | (b) the base or repeater station has been inspected to the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:353 | satisfaction of an authorised officer; and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:354 | (c) the Authority approves the change.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 10 (amendment of licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:338-354)
GIVEN `the amendment transfers the location of a station other than a portable or mobile station, or changes the radio-communication equipment comprised in the station` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the station has been satisfactorily inspected by an authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority has approved the transfer or change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 10(1): the amendment may be made` MEANS
    (NOT `the amendment transfers the location of a station other than a portable or mobile station, or changes the radio-communication equipment comprised in the station`)
    OR (`the station has been satisfactorily inspected by an authorised officer` AND `the Authority has approved the transfer or change`)

GIVEN `an authorised officer inspects a station or network under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 10(2): the fee in dollars the Authority may impose for the inspection` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `an authorised officer inspects a station or network under paragraph (1)` THEN JUST 70
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `the licensee has notified the Authority of the change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the base or repeater station has been inspected to the satisfaction of an authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority approves the change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 10(3): the amendment for a change in the base or repeater station of the network may be made` MEANS
    `the licensee has notified the Authority of the change` AND `the base or repeater station has been inspected to the satisfaction of an authorised officer` AND `the Authority approves the change`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:356 | Renewal of licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:357 | 11. Every application for the renewal of a licence under these
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:358 | Regulations shall be in such form and manner as the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:359 | require.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 11 (renewal of licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:356-359)
GIVEN `the application for renewal is in the form and manner the Authority requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 11: the application for renewal is in order` MEANS `the application for renewal is in the form and manner the Authority requires`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:361 | Suspension and revocation of licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:362 | 12.—(1) The Authority may suspend or revoke a licence granted
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:363 | under these Regulations by notice in writing addressed to the licensee
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:364 | on the grounds that the licensee had in his application for the licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:365 | furnished false, misleading or inaccurate information or that there has
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:366 | been misuse of equipment or failure to comply with any of the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:367 | provisions of the Act, these Regulations or with any condition of the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:368 | licence.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:369 | (2) Where a licence is suspended or revoked by the Authority, the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:370 | licensee shall surrender the licence to the Authority if requested by
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:371 | the Authority within such time as the Authority may specify.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:372 | (3) Where a licence is suspended or revoked by the Authority or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:373 | where a licence is terminated by a licensee, no compensation shall be
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:374 | paid by the Authority to the licensee and no fee or part thereof shall,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:375 | unless provided for in the licence, be refunded by the Authority to the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:376 | licensee in respect of the unexpired period of such licence.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 12 (suspension and revocation of licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:361-376)
GIVEN `the licensee furnished false, misleading or inaccurate information in the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been misuse of equipment or a failure to comply with a provision of the Act or the Regulations or a condition of the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 12(1): the Authority may suspend or revoke the licence by notice in writing` MEANS
    `the licensee furnished false, misleading or inaccurate information in the application` OR `there has been misuse of equipment or a failure to comply with a provision of the Act or the Regulations or a condition of the licence`

GIVEN `the Authority requests surrender within a time it specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee surrenders the licence within that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 12(2): the licensee has done what the regulation requires` MEANS
    (NOT `the Authority requests surrender within a time it specifies`) OR `the licensee surrenders the licence within that time`

GIVEN `the licence is suspended or revoked by the Authority, or terminated by the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence provides for a refund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 12(3): no compensation is paid and no fee is refunded for the unexpired period` MEANS
    `the licence is suspended or revoked by the Authority, or terminated by the licensee` AND (NOT `the licence provides for a refund`)

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:378 | Return of licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:379 | 13.—(1) When a licensee ceases to operate a station or network or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:380 | when a licence ceases to be valid, the licensee shall return the licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:383 | to the Authority for cancellation and the Authority may require the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:384 | licensee to seal, disable or dismantle the radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:385 | equipment comprised in the station or network in the presence of any
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:386 | authorised officer.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:387 | (2) Unless authorised by the Authority, the licensee may only
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:388 | dispose of or offer the station, network or any radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:389 | equipment comprised therein for sale if it has first been sealed,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:390 | disabled or dismantled.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:391 | (3) Where any radio-communication equipment has been sealed,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:392 | disabled or dismantled under paragraph (1), no person shall, unless
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:393 | authorised by the Authority, break or tamper with the seal or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:394 | reassemble the equipment, as the case may be.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 13 (return of licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:378-394)
GIVEN `the licensee ceases to operate the station or network, or the licence ceases to be valid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee returns the licence to the Authority for cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 13(1): the licensee has done what the regulation requires` MEANS
    (NOT `the licensee ceases to operate the station or network, or the licence ceases to be valid`) OR `the licensee returns the licence to the Authority for cancellation`

GIVEN `the station, network or equipment has first been sealed, disabled or dismantled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority authorised the disposal or offer for sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 13(2): the licensee may dispose of or offer for sale the station, network or equipment` MEANS
    `the station, network or equipment has first been sealed, disabled or dismantled` OR `the Authority authorised the disposal or offer for sale`

GIVEN `the equipment has been sealed, disabled or dismantled under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person breaks or tampers with the seal or reassembles the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority authorised it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 13(3): the person contravenes the regulation` MEANS
    `the equipment has been sealed, disabled or dismantled under paragraph (1)` AND `the person breaks or tampers with the seal or reassembles the equipment` AND (NOT `the Authority authorised it`)

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:396 | Licensee not exempted from other laws
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:397 | 14. The grant of any licence under these Regulations shall not
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:398 | exempt the licensee from obtaining any other permits, licences or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:399 | other authorisations required by law for or in connection with the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:400 | installation, operation or use of any station or network.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 14 (licensee not exempted from other laws) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:396-400)
GIVEN `a licence has been granted under the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another permit, licence or authorisation is required by law for or in connection with the installation, operation or use of the station or network` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 14: the licensee must still obtain the other permit, licence or authorisation` MEANS
    `a licence has been granted under the Regulations` AND `another permit, licence or authorisation is required by law for or in connection with the installation, operation or use of the station or network`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:402 | Power of Authority to change or withdraw frequency
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:403 | 15. The Authority may, in its discretion and without paying
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:404 | compensation and upon giving such notice as it may consider
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:405 | appropriate, change or withdraw any frequency allocated to the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:406 | licensee in a licence without assigning any reason therefor.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 15 (power of Authority to change or withdraw frequency) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:402-406)
GIVEN `the frequency was allocated to the licensee in a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority gives such notice as it considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 15: the Authority may, without compensation and without assigning a reason, change or withdraw the frequency` MEANS
    `the frequency was allocated to the licensee in a licence` AND `the Authority gives such notice as it considers appropriate`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:408 | Secrecy
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:409 | 16.—(1) Except as may be provided by section 78 (2) of the Act, no
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:410 | person shall intercept or acquaint himself with the contents of any
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:411 | radio-communication other than those transmitted for general
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:412 | information or for the information of licensees belonging to the same
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:413 | licensed network.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:414 | (2) Except as otherwise provided in these Regulations or by the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:415 | terms and conditions of a station or network licence granted for
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:416 | the reception of radio-communications only, every person having
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:417 | access to radio-communications shall hold strictly secret all radio-
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:418 | communications, other than those transmitted for general
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:419 | information, which may pass through his hands or come to his
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:420 | knowledge.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:422 | (3) Such person shall not, directly or indirectly, disclose the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:423 | contents thereof except to a person entitled to become acquainted
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:424 | with the radio-communications or to an authorised officer or to a
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:425 | court and shall not make other use of such radio-communications.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:426 | (4) No person having unauthorised access to radio-
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:427 | communications shall print or publish or cause to be printed or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:428 | published in any newspaper, pamphlet, book or document, any
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:429 | radio-communication that may pass through his hands or come to his
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:430 | knowledge, whether such radio-communication be for private or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:431 | general reception.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 16 (secrecy) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:408-431)
GIVEN `the person intercepts or acquaints himself with the contents of a radio-communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the radio-communication was transmitted for general information or for the information of licensees belonging to the same licensed network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 78(2) of the Act provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 16(1): the person contravenes the regulation` MEANS
    `the person intercepts or acquaints himself with the contents of a radio-communication`
    AND (NOT `the radio-communication was transmitted for general information or for the information of licensees belonging to the same licensed network`)
    AND (NOT `section 78(2) of the Act provides otherwise`)

GIVEN `the person has access to radio-communications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the radio-communication was transmitted for general information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds it strictly secret` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms of a station or network licence granted for the reception of radio-communications only provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 16(2): the person is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    (NOT `the person has access to radio-communications`) OR `the radio-communication was transmitted for general information` OR `the terms of a station or network licence granted for the reception of radio-communications only provide otherwise` OR `the person holds it strictly secret`

GIVEN `the person discloses the contents or makes other use of the radio-communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is to a person entitled to become acquainted with it, to an authorised officer or to a court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 16(3): the person contravenes the regulation` MEANS
    `the person discloses the contents or makes other use of the radio-communication` AND (NOT `the disclosure is to a person entitled to become acquainted with it, to an authorised officer or to a court`)

GIVEN `the person has unauthorised access to radio-communications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person prints or publishes it or causes it to be printed or published in a newspaper, pamphlet, book or document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 16(4): the person contravenes the regulation` MEANS
    `the person has unauthorised access to radio-communications` AND `the person prints or publishes it or causes it to be printed or published in a newspaper, pamphlet, book or document`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:433 | Station and network to be used for lawful purposes
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:434 | 17. No person shall operate or use any station or network for or in
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:435 | furtherance of any unlawful purpose.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 17 (station and network to be used for lawful purposes) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:433-435)
GIVEN `the person operates or uses the station or network for or in furtherance of an unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 17: the person contravenes the regulation` MEANS `the person operates or uses the station or network for or in furtherance of an unlawful purpose`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:437 | Technical requirements
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:438 | 18.—(1) Before a licence is granted, the applicant shall satisfy the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:439 | Authority that the station or network in respect of which the licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:440 | is to be granted conforms to such technical requirements as may be
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:441 | imposed by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:442 | (2) All equipment comprised in a station or network shall be
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:443 | approved by the Authority before use.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:444 | (3) Every station or network in respect of which an application for
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:445 | a licence has been made or for which a licence has been granted may
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:446 | at any time be inspected and tested by an authorised officer.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 18 (technical requirements) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:437-446)
GIVEN `the applicant has satisfied the Authority that the station or network conforms to the technical requirements imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 18(1): a licence may be granted` MEANS `the applicant has satisfied the Authority that the station or network conforms to the technical requirements imposed`

GIVEN `the equipment comprised in the station or network has been approved by the Authority before use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 18(2): the equipment may be used` MEANS `the equipment comprised in the station or network has been approved by the Authority before use`

GIVEN `an application for a licence has been made for the station or network, or a licence has been granted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 18(3): an authorised officer may at any time inspect and test the station or network` MEANS `an application for a licence has been made for the station or network, or a licence has been granted`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:448 | Restrictions on transmission
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:449 | 19.—(1) The transmission of superfluous signals by a station or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:450 | network is prohibited.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:451 | (2) No test, trial or practical transmission shall be permitted except
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:452 | in such circumstances as to preclude the possibility of interference
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:453 | with any other station or network.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:454 | (3) All tests, unless prior approval from the Authority has been
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:455 | obtained, shall be conducted on dummy load.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:456 | (4) No person shall transmit —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:457 | (a) any message containing indecent, obscene or offensive
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:458 | language;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:461 | (b) any message for an improper or illegal purpose;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:462 | (c) any message which interferes with the operation of any
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:463 | authorised station or network; or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:464 | (d) any message which, to his knowledge, is false or misleading
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:465 | and likely to prejudice the efficiency of any life-service or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:466 | endanger the safety of any person or of a place or premises,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:467 | vessel, aircraft or vehicle.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:468 | (5) A licensee shall ensure that a station or network is worked in
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:469 | a manner which is safe and which does not impair or interfere with —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:470 | (a) any Armed Forces Communication; or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:471 | (b) the efficient and convenient working or maintenance of any
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:472 | other station or network, or telecommunication system or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:473 | service in Singapore authorised by the Authority under the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:474 | Act or these Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:475 | (6) A licensee shall cease operating his station or network and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:476 | shall take any other immediate action which the Authority stipulates
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:477 | as soon as it observes, or when it has been informed by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:478 | or any other competent authority, that the working of his station or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:479 | network causes interference to radio-communication.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:480 | (7) The licensee shall, where so directed by the Authority in
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:481 | writing, cease to operate any or all of the equipment comprised in his
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:482 | station for such period or periods of time as may be required by the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:483 | Authority for the purposes of investigation of interference to
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:484 | radio-communications.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 19 (restrictions on transmission) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:448-484)
GIVEN `the station or network transmits superfluous signals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the test, trial or practical transmission is in circumstances that preclude the possibility of interference with any other station or network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the test is conducted on dummy load, or the Authority's prior approval has been obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person transmits a message containing indecent, obscene or offensive language, or sent for an improper or illegal purpose, or interfering with the operation of any authorised station or network, or known to be false or misleading and likely to prejudice the efficiency of any life-service or endanger safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 19(1) to (4): the person is meeting the regulation` MEANS
        (NOT `the station or network transmits superfluous signals`)
    AND `the test, trial or practical transmission is in circumstances that preclude the possibility of interference with any other station or network`
    AND `the test is conducted on dummy load, or the Authority's prior approval has been obtained`
    AND (NOT `the person transmits a message containing indecent, obscene or offensive language, or sent for an improper or illegal purpose, or interfering with the operation of any authorised station or network, or known to be false or misleading and likely to prejudice the efficiency of any life-service or endanger safety`)

GIVEN `the licensee ensures the station or network is worked in a manner which is safe and which does not impair or interfere with any Armed Forces Communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee ensures it does not impair or interfere with the efficient and convenient working or maintenance of any other station or network, or telecommunication system or service in Singapore authorised under the Act or the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 19(5): the licensee is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    `the licensee ensures the station or network is worked in a manner which is safe and which does not impair or interfere with any Armed Forces Communication`
    AND `the licensee ensures it does not impair or interfere with the efficient and convenient working or maintenance of any other station or network, or telecommunication system or service in Singapore authorised under the Act or the Regulations`

GIVEN `the working of the station or network causes interference to radio-communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee has observed it or been informed by the Authority or another competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee ceases operating and takes the other immediate action the Authority stipulates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 19(6): the licensee is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    (NOT (`the working of the station or network causes interference to radio-communication` AND `the licensee has observed it or been informed by the Authority or another competent authority`)) OR `the licensee ceases operating and takes the other immediate action the Authority stipulates`

GIVEN `the Authority directs in writing that equipment cease to operate for the period required for investigation of interference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee ceases to operate the equipment for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 19(7): the licensee is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    (NOT `the Authority directs in writing that equipment cease to operate for the period required for investigation of interference`) OR `the licensee ceases to operate the equipment for the period`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:486 | International Telecommunication Convention
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:487 | 20.—(1) The provisions of the International Telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:488 | Convention and the regulations for the time being in force thereunder
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:489 | shall, so far as they are applicable, apply to any station or network
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:490 | established or operated in Singapore and to any message transmitted
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:491 | or received by such station or network.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:492 | (2) The Authority may, in its discretion, waive the application of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:493 | any of the provisions or regulations to any station, network or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:494 | message.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 20 (International Telecommunication Convention) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:486-494)
GIVEN `the station or network is established or operated in Singapore, or the message is transmitted or received by it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority has waived the application of the provision or regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 20: the provisions of the International Telecommunication Convention apply, so far as applicable` MEANS
    `the station or network is established or operated in Singapore, or the message is transmitted or received by it` AND (NOT `the Authority has waived the application of the provision or regulation`)

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:496 | Inspection of radio-communication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:497 | 21.—(1) For the purpose of ensuring that the Act, these
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:498 | Regulations and any condition of a licence granted hereunder are
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:500 | complied with, an authorised officer shall be entitled, upon
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:501 | production of proof of identity, to enter any building, premises,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:502 | compound or other place, vehicle, vessel or aircraft where a station or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:503 | network is installed, or is being installed and may inspect, examine or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:504 | test any equipment comprised therein.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:505 | (2) The owner or occupier of such building, premises, compound
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:506 | or other place, vehicle, vessel or aircraft shall allow the authorised
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:507 | officer to enter and inspect such station, network or equipment.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:508 | (3) Where the owner or user of a station or network requests the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:509 | Authority to inspect, for the second or subsequent time, any station
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:510 | or network licensed or to be licensed under these Regulations to
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:511 | verify that the station or network or any equipment comprised
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:512 | therein is designed, constructed, installed, established, maintained or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:513 | operated in accordance with any of the provisions of the Act, these
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:514 | Regulations or any condition of the licence, the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:515 | impose a fee of $70 for the inspection.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 21 (inspection of radio-communication equipment) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:496-515)
GIVEN `the authorised officer produced proof of identity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to ensure that the Act, the Regulations and the conditions of a licence are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 21(1): the authorised officer is entitled to enter the building, premises, compound or other place, vehicle, vessel or aircraft where a station or network is installed or is being installed, and inspect, examine or test any equipment` MEANS
    `the authorised officer produced proof of identity` AND `the purpose is to ensure that the Act, the Regulations and the conditions of a licence are complied with`

GIVEN `the owner or occupier allows the authorised officer to enter and inspect the station, network or equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 21(2): the owner or occupier is meeting the regulation` MEANS `the owner or occupier allows the authorised officer to enter and inspect the station, network or equipment`

GIVEN `the owner or user requests the Authority to inspect for the second or subsequent time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 21(3): the fee in dollars the Authority may impose for the inspection` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the owner or user requests the Authority to inspect for the second or subsequent time` THEN JUST 70
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:517 | Inspection of licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:518 | 22.—(1) A police officer not below the rank of sergeant or an
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:519 | authorised officer shall be entitled, upon production of proof of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:520 | identity, to examine the licence of a station or network or if it is not
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:521 | immediately available, require its production at the office of the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:522 | Authority or a named police station within a reasonable period.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:523 | (2) A police officer not below the rank of sergeant or an
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:524 | authorised officer may search and seize any radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:525 | equipment which is found by him in any place, vehicle, vessel or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:526 | aircraft without a licence.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 22 (inspection of licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:517-526)
GIVEN `the person is a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, or an authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer produced proof of identity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 22(1): the officer is entitled to examine the licence of the station or network, or to require its production at the office of the Authority or a named police station within a reasonable period` MEANS
    `the person is a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, or an authorised officer` AND `the officer produced proof of identity`

GIVEN `the person is a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, or an authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the radio-communication equipment is found in a place, vehicle, vessel or aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is without a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 22(2): the officer may search and seize the radio-communication equipment` MEANS
    `the person is a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, or an authorised officer` AND `the radio-communication equipment is found in a place, vehicle, vessel or aircraft` AND `it is without a licence`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:528 | Fees
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:529 | 23.—(1) The fee payable for a station licence is specified in Part I
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:530 | of the Second Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:531 | (2) The application and processing fees for use of a frequency in
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:532 | the course of operating or using a station or network under these
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:533 | Regulations are specified in Part II of the Second Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:534 | (3) The annual fee payable for use of a frequency in the course of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:535 | operating or using a station or network under these Regulations is
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:536 | specified in Part III of the Second Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:539 | (4) The Authority may, in the interest of spectrum economy and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:540 | after considering the re-usability of a frequency, the area of coverage
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:541 | involved and the period of use of an assigned frequency, reduce the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:542 | application and pocessing fees payable under paragraph (2) or the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:543 | annual fee payable under paragraph (3) or both.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:544 | (5) For any multi-channel radio-communication equipment used
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:545 | for transmitting or receiving, the frequency charge payable shall be in
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:546 | accordance with the bandwidth of frequencies assigned as specified in
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:547 | Part III of the Second Schedule.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 23 (fees) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:528-547)
GIVEN `the Authority considers the re-usability of the frequency, the area of coverage and the period of use of the assigned frequency, in the interest of spectrum economy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 23(4): the Authority may reduce the application and processing fees, or the annual fee, or both` MEANS `the Authority considers the re-usability of the frequency, the area of coverage and the period of use of the assigned frequency, in the interest of spectrum economy`

GIVEN `the multi-channel radio-communication equipment is used for transmitting or receiving` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 23(5): the frequency charge is in accordance with the bandwidth of frequencies assigned, as Part III of the Second Schedule specifies` MEANS `the multi-channel radio-communication equipment is used for transmitting or receiving`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:549 | Network licence fees
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:550 | 24. The fee payable for a network licence is specified in Part I of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:551 | the Second Schedule.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 24 (network licence fees) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:549-551)
GIVEN `the licence is a network licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 24: the fee is the one Part I of the Second Schedule specifies` MEANS `the licence is a network licence`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:553 | Late payment fee
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:554 | 25. All fees shall be paid in advance and if any fee remains unpaid
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:555 | 7 days after the date on which a licence should have been renewed,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:556 | the following late payment fee shall be charged:
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:557 | (a) where the licence is renewed after 7 days but less than
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:558 | 15 days following the expiration of the previous licence, a
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:559 | sum of $10;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:560 | (b) where the licence is renewed after 14 days but less than
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:561 | 31 days following the expiration of the previous licence, a
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:562 | sum of $20; and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:563 | (c) where the licence is renewed after 30 days following the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:564 | expiration of the previous licence, a sum of $50.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:566 | PART III
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:567 | CLASSES OF LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:568 | Network Licence
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 25 (late payment fee) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:553-568)
GIVEN `days after the expiration of the previous licence on which the licence is renewed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 25: the late payment fee in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `days after the expiration of the previous licence on which the licence is renewed` AT MOST 7 THEN 0
           IF `days after the expiration of the previous licence on which the licence is renewed` LESS THAN 15 THEN 10
           IF `days after the expiration of the previous licence on which the licence is renewed` LESS THAN 31 THEN 20
           OTHERWISE 50

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:570 | Network licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:571 | 26.—(1) The Authority may grant the following classes of network
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:572 | licences:
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:573 | (a) localised private network licence;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:574 | (b) wide-area private network licence; and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:575 | (c) public mobile network licence.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:577 | (2) The grant of a private network licence shall not, unless the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:578 | Authority otherwise determines, authorise the licensee to provide,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:579 | directly or indirectly, any telecommunication service to the general
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:580 | public.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:581 | (3) A network licence shall only be granted in respect of a network
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:582 | which meets all technical standards and any other requirements which
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:583 | the Authority may, from time to time, stipulate.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:584 | (4) The Authority may refuse to grant a localised private network
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:585 | licence or wide-area private network licence if it is satisfied that —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:586 | (a) the licensee failed to meet the minimum channel loading
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:587 | criteria set by the Authority from time to time for the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:588 | network; or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:589 | (b) the radio-communication service that is, or is intended to be,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:590 | provided by or through the network may be adequately
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:591 | provided by or through a public telecommunication system
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:592 | or by any other means.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 26 (network licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:570-592)
GIVEN class IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 26(1): the Authority may grant the class of network licence` MEANS
    class EQUALS "localised private network licence" OR class EQUALS "wide-area private network licence" OR class EQUALS "public mobile network licence"

GIVEN `the network is a private network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority otherwise determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 26(2): the grant authorises the licensee to provide a telecommunication service to the general public, directly or indirectly` MEANS
    `the network is a private network` AND `the Authority otherwise determined`

GIVEN `the network meets all technical standards and any other requirements the Authority stipulates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 26(3): a network licence may be granted` MEANS `the network meets all technical standards and any other requirements the Authority stipulates`

GIVEN `the licensee failed to meet the minimum channel loading criteria set by the Authority for the network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service may be adequately provided by or through a public telecommunication system or by any other means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 26(4): the Authority may refuse to grant a localised private network licence or wide-area private network licence` MEANS
    `the licensee failed to meet the minimum channel loading criteria set by the Authority for the network` OR `the service may be adequately provided by or through a public telecommunication system or by any other means`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:594 | Ship Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:595 | 27.—(1) A Ship Station Licence may be granted by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:596 | if —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:597 | (a) the ship has a valid internationally recognised Safety Radio
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:598 | certificate;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:599 | (b) the station is operated by an appropriate number and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:600 | category of radio operators holding a Certificate of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:601 | Competency granted under the Radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:602 | (Certificates of Competency for Ship Station Operators)
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:603 | Regulations (Rg 2) or a competent foreign authority
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:604 | recognised by the Authority, except where the vessel is used
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:605 | solely or principally for pleasure purposes;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:606 | (c) the ship has an accounting authority acceptable to the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:607 | Authority; and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:608 | (d) the ship complies with such other requirements as may be
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:609 | determined by the Authority from time to time.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:610 | (2) A person who is unable to furnish all the information required
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:611 | by the Authority in the application form for a Ship Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:612 | may, upon payment of the prescribed fee and upon satisfying such
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:613 | other requirements as may be determined by the Authority, be
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:616 | granted a Provisional Ship Station Licence which shall be valid for
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:617 | such period and subject to such conditions as may be determined by
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:618 | the Authority.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 27 (Ship Station Licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:594-618)
GIVEN `the ship has a valid internationally recognised Safety Radio certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the station is operated by an appropriate number and category of radio operators holding a Certificate of Competency, or the vessel is used solely or principally for pleasure purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship has an accounting authority acceptable to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship complies with such other requirements as the Authority determines` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 27(1): a Ship Station Licence may be granted` MEANS
        `the ship has a valid internationally recognised Safety Radio certificate`
    AND `the station is operated by an appropriate number and category of radio operators holding a Certificate of Competency, or the vessel is used solely or principally for pleasure purposes`
    AND `the ship has an accounting authority acceptable to the Authority`
    AND `the ship complies with such other requirements as the Authority determines`

GIVEN `the person is unable to furnish all the information required in the application form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed fee has been paid and the other requirements of the Authority are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 27(2): the person may be granted a Provisional Ship Station Licence` MEANS
    `the person is unable to furnish all the information required in the application form` AND `the prescribed fee has been paid and the other requirements of the Authority are satisfied`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:620 | Restrictions on grant of Ship Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:621 | 28. A Ship Station Licence shall only be granted in respect of a
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:622 | ship, including its lifeboats, which is registered or licensed by the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:623 | competent authority in Singapore.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 28 (restrictions on grant of Ship Station Licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:620-623)
GIVEN `the ship, including its lifeboats, is registered or licensed by the competent authority in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 28: a Ship Station Licence may be granted in respect of the ship` MEANS `the ship, including its lifeboats, is registered or licensed by the competent authority in Singapore`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:625 | Compliance with Radio Regulations, Authority’s requirements, etc.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:626 | 29. A Ship Station licensee shall —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:627 | (a) provide on board the ship all documents either considered
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:628 | necessary by the Authority or required under the Radio
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:629 | Regulations for the efficient operation of the ship station;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:630 | and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:631 | (b) comply with the working procedures set out in the Radio
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:632 | Regulations and with such other requirements as the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:633 | Authority may determine.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 29 (compliance with Radio Regulations, Authority's requirements, etc.) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:625-633)
GIVEN `the licensee provides on board the documents the Authority considers necessary or the Radio Regulations require` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee complies with the working procedures set out in the Radio Regulations and the other requirements the Authority determines` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 29: the Ship Station licensee is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    `the licensee provides on board the documents the Authority considers necessary or the Radio Regulations require` AND `the licensee complies with the working procedures set out in the Radio Regulations and the other requirements the Authority determines`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:635 | Equipment not to cause interference
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:636 | 30.—(1) A station on board any ship in the waters of Singapore
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:637 | shall be operated in such manner as not to interfere with —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:638 | (a) any Armed Forces Communication; or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:639 | (b) the efficient and convenient working of a government or of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:640 | any licensed station or network in Singapore.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:641 | (2) A station on board any ship shall cease operation as soon as the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:642 | crew of the ship observes, or when the crew has been informed by the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:643 | Authority that the working of the ship station causes interference to
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:644 | radio-communication.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 30 (equipment not to cause interference) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:635-644)
GIVEN `the station on board a ship in the waters of Singapore is operated so as not to interfere with Armed Forces Communication or with the efficient and convenient working of a government or licensed station or network` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 30(1): the station is operated as the regulation requires` MEANS `the station on board a ship in the waters of Singapore is operated so as not to interfere with Armed Forces Communication or with the efficient and convenient working of a government or licensed station or network`

GIVEN `the crew observes, or has been informed by the Authority, that the working of the ship station causes interference to radio-communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the station ceases operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 30(2): the station is operated as the regulation requires` MEANS
    (NOT `the crew observes, or has been informed by the Authority, that the working of the ship station causes interference to radio-communication`) OR `the station ceases operation`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:646 | Restrictions on use of equipment while in territorial waters
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:647 | 31.—(1) No station on board a ship shall be used while the ship is
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:648 | within the territorial waters of Singapore.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:649 | (2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), a station on board a ship,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:650 | whether licensed by the Authority or by a foreign competent
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:651 | authority, may be used while the ship is within the territorial waters
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:652 | of Singapore for the purposes of —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:654 | (a) safety of navigation, life or property or for any other
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:655 | purposes as may be authorised by the Authority; and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:656 | (b) communication on such frequency bands as may be
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:657 | specifically authorised by the Authority, subject to such
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:658 | conditions as may be determined by the Authority, provided
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:659 | that the use of such station shall not cause interference to the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:660 | working of any other authorised station or network.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:662 | Aircraft Station Licence
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 31 (restrictions on use of equipment while in territorial waters) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:646-662)
GIVEN `the ship is within the territorial waters of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for the safety of navigation, life or property or another purpose the Authority authorises, or for communication on frequency bands the Authority specifically authorises subject to its conditions, and does not cause interference to the working of any other authorised station or network` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 31: the station on board the ship may be used` MEANS
    (NOT `the ship is within the territorial waters of Singapore`) OR `the use is for the safety of navigation, life or property or another purpose the Authority authorises, or for communication on frequency bands the Authority specifically authorises subject to its conditions, and does not cause interference to the working of any other authorised station or network`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:664 | Restrictions on grant of Aircraft Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:665 | 32. An Aircraft Station Licence shall be granted only in respect of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:666 | a commercial or privately-owned aircraft registered in Singapore.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 32 (restrictions on grant of Aircraft Station Licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:664-666)
GIVEN `the aircraft is a commercial or privately-owned aircraft registered in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 32: an Aircraft Station Licence may be granted in respect of the aircraft` MEANS `the aircraft is a commercial or privately-owned aircraft registered in Singapore`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:668 | Duty of licensee in respect of equipment, Radio Regulations, etc.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:669 | 33.—(1) All equipment comprised in a station on board any
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:670 | aircraft shall be approved by the Director-General of the Civil
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:671 | Aviation Authority of Singapore and a certificate to this effect shall
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:672 | accompany the application for the licence.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:673 | (2) The licensee of a station on board an aircraft shall observe the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:674 | provisions of the Radio Regulations and any other local or interna-
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:675 | tional rules and regulations applicable to stations on board an
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:676 | aircraft.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 33 (duty of licensee in respect of equipment, Radio Regulations, etc.) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:668-676)
GIVEN `the equipment comprised in the station on board the aircraft is approved by the Director-General of the Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore and a certificate to that effect accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee observes the Radio Regulations and the other local or international rules applicable to stations on board an aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 33: the aircraft station licensee is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    `the equipment comprised in the station on board the aircraft is approved by the Director-General of the Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore and a certificate to that effect accompanies the application` AND `the licensee observes the Radio Regulations and the other local or international rules applicable to stations on board an aircraft`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:678 | Restrictions on use of aircraft station
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:679 | 34. No station fitted in an aircraft shall be operated or used while
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:680 | such aircraft is at rest on land or on water in Singapore except —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:681 | (a) in exceptional cases or in time of emergency or distress;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:682 | (b) if communication by means of a telecommunication line
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:683 | system is not available, for communication in exceptional
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:684 | circumstances on matters relating to air navigation and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:685 | services with the nearest aeronautical station, or, if
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:686 | communication with such station is impracticable, with any
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:687 | other station; or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:688 | (c) for the purpose of carrying out experimental tests, with the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:689 | written consent of and subject to such conditions as may be
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:690 | determined by the Authority or for the purpose of carrying
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:696 | out functional tests to determine the serviceability of the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:697 | station, provided that such tests shall not be carried out on
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:698 | international distress frequencies.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:700 | Amateur Station Licence
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 34 (restrictions on use of aircraft station) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:678-700)
GIVEN `the aircraft is at rest on land or on water in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in exceptional cases or in time of emergency or distress` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for communication on matters relating to air navigation and services, where communication by a telecommunication line system is not available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for experimental tests with the Authority's written consent, or functional tests to determine the serviceability of the station, not on international distress frequencies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 34: the station fitted in the aircraft may be operated or used` MEANS
    (NOT `the aircraft is at rest on land or on water in Singapore`) OR `the use is in exceptional cases or in time of emergency or distress` OR `the use is for communication on matters relating to air navigation and services, where communication by a telecommunication line system is not available` OR `the use is for experimental tests with the Authority's written consent, or functional tests to determine the serviceability of the station, not on international distress frequencies`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:702 | Amateur Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:703 | 35.—(1) The Authority may grant the following classes of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:704 | Amateur Station Licence to qualified or approved persons interested
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:705 | in the operation of radio-communication equipment solely for
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:706 | pleasure and for the furtherance of radio-communication techniques
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:707 | and not for pecuniary gain:
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:708 | (a) General Class;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:709 | (b) Restricted Class; and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:710 | (c) any other class of licence which the Authority considers
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:711 | appropriate.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:712 | (2) An Amateur Station Licence may only be granted to a natural
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:713 | person and shall not authorise the use of radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:714 | equipment by the licensee’s employees.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 35 (Amateur Station Licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:702-714)
GIVEN class IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 35(1): the Authority may grant the class of Amateur Station Licence` MEANS
    class EQUALS "General Class" OR class EQUALS "Restricted Class" OR class EQUALS "any other class of licence which the Authority considers appropriate"

GIVEN `the applicant is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 35(2): an Amateur Station Licence may be granted, and does not authorise use by the licensee's employees` MEANS `the applicant is a natural person`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:716 | Age restrictions
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:717 | 36.—(1) An Amateur Station Licence shall not be granted to a
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:718 | person below the age of 16 years.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:719 | (2) Any application for an Amateur Station Licence by an
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:720 | applicant below the age of 21 years shall be countersigned by the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:721 | applicant’s parent, guardian or by any other person approved by the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:722 | Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:723 | (3) An Amateur Station licensee between the ages of 16 and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:724 | 21 years may only operate or use any Amateur Station if supervised
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:725 | by a qualified person approved by the Authority and who has agreed
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:726 | to supervise the licensee, and that qualified person shall ensure that
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:727 | the licensee observes and complies with all duties and obligations
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:728 | specified in the licence and in these Regulations.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 36 (age restrictions) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:716-728)
GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 36(1): an Amateur Station Licence may be granted to a person of that age` MEANS `age in years` AT LEAST 16

GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the application is countersigned by the applicant's parent, guardian or another person approved by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 36(2): the application is in order` MEANS `age in years` AT LEAST 21 OR `the application is countersigned by the applicant's parent, guardian or another person approved by the Authority`

GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the licensee is supervised by a qualified person approved by the Authority who has agreed to supervise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 36(3): the licensee may operate or use an Amateur Station` MEANS `age in years` AT LEAST 21 OR `the licensee is supervised by a qualified person approved by the Authority who has agreed to supervise`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:730 | Qualifications
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:731 | 37.—(1) An applicant for an Amateur Station Licence shall, unless
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:732 | exempted by the Authority —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:734 | (a) have passed the Radio Amateur Examination set by the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:735 | Authority; or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:736 | (b) be in possession of an Amateur Radio Certificate acceptable
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:737 | to the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:738 | (2) The fee payable to sit for the Radio Amateur Examination
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:739 | referred to in paragraph (1) is specified in the Third Schedule.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 37 (qualifications) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:730-739)
GIVEN `the Authority exempted the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant has passed the Radio Amateur Examination set by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is in possession of an Amateur Radio Certificate acceptable to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 37(1): the applicant is qualified` MEANS
    `the Authority exempted the applicant` OR `the applicant has passed the Radio Amateur Examination set by the Authority` OR `the applicant is in possession of an Amateur Radio Certificate acceptable to the Authority`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:741 | Conditions
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:742 | 38. An Amateur Station licensee shall observe the following
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:743 | conditions:
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:744 | (a) the station shall only be operated at locations approved by
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:745 | the Authority;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:746 | (b) the station shall in all cases be operated by the licensee or by
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:747 | persons named in the licence;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:748 | (c) the station and all equipment used or intended to be used by
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:749 | the licensee shall be erected, fixed, placed and used, so as not
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:750 | to interfere with the efficient and convenient working of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:751 | other authorised stations;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:752 | (d) the licensee shall identify himself by the transmission of the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:753 | callsign assigned to him by the Authority at the beginning
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:754 | and end of each transmission;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:755 | (e) any change in the approved location, equipment, mast or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:756 | antenna system must be approved by the Authority prior to
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:757 | the change being made;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:758 | (f) the licensee shall obtain the approval of all relevant
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:759 | authorities before erecting any mast or antenna to be used in
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:760 | connection with the operation of the station; and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:761 | (g) the licensee shall —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:762 | (i) keep a running record of all transmission periods
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:763 | showing the date and time of each period of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:764 | transmission and the frequency and type of emission
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:765 | employed;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:766 | (ii) preserve the record of each entry made for one year;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:767 | and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:768 | (iii) make the record mentioned in sub-paragraph (ii)
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:769 | available for inspection at all reasonable times by an
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:770 | authorised officer.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 38 (conditions) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:741-770)
GIVEN `the station is only operated at locations approved by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the station is operated by the licensee or by persons named in the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the station and equipment are erected, fixed, placed and used so as not to interfere with the efficient and convenient working of other authorised stations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee identifies himself by the callsign assigned by the Authority at the beginning and end of each transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any change in the approved location, equipment, mast or antenna system is approved by the Authority before it is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee obtained the approval of all relevant authorities before erecting any mast or antenna` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee keeps a running record of all transmission periods, preserves each entry for one year and makes the record available for inspection by an authorised officer at all reasonable times` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 38(a) to (g): the Amateur Station licensee is meeting the conditions` MEANS
        `the station is only operated at locations approved by the Authority`
    AND `the station is operated by the licensee or by persons named in the licence`
    AND `the station and equipment are erected, fixed, placed and used so as not to interfere with the efficient and convenient working of other authorised stations`
    AND `the licensee identifies himself by the callsign assigned by the Authority at the beginning and end of each transmission`
    AND `any change in the approved location, equipment, mast or antenna system is approved by the Authority before it is made`
    AND `the licensee obtained the approval of all relevant authorities before erecting any mast or antenna`
    AND `the licensee keeps a running record of all transmission periods, preserves each entry for one year and makes the record available for inspection by an authorised officer at all reasonable times`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:775 | Prohibition on use of encryption devices
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:776 | 39. An Amateur Station licensee may not make use of encryption
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:777 | devices or equipment in the operation or use of any station.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 39 (prohibition on use of encryption devices) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:775-777)
GIVEN `the licensee makes use of encryption devices or equipment in the operation or use of a station` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 39: the Amateur Station licensee contravenes the regulation` MEANS `the licensee makes use of encryption devices or equipment in the operation or use of a station`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:779 | Restrictions on transmission
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:780 | 40.—(1) Messages transmitted through an Amateur Station shall
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:781 | be in plain language and shall relate solely to the licensee’s
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:782 | experiments or personal affairs (not being business affairs), or to the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:783 | personal affairs of the person with whom the licensee is communi-
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:784 | cating.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:785 | (2) An Amateur Station shall not be used for transmitting news,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:786 | advertisements, communications of a business or non-experimental
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:787 | character, messages for pecuniary reward or messages for or on
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:788 | behalf of a third party.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:789 | (3) Except with the written permission of the Authority, no
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:790 | licensee of an Amateur Station shall call or transmit to any station
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:791 | other than an Amateur Station.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:792 | (4) Messages may only be exchanged with another Amateur
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:793 | Station, except where prohibited by law.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:794 | (5) Transmission shall not commence without listening in on the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:795 | frequency to be used in order to ascertain that no interference is
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:796 | likely to be caused to any other station which may be functioning.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 40 (restrictions on transmission) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:779-796)
GIVEN `the messages are in plain language and relate solely to the licensee's experiments or personal affairs (not business affairs) or those of the person with whom the licensee is communicating` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Amateur Station is used for transmitting news, advertisements, communications of a business or non-experimental character, messages for pecuniary reward or messages for or on behalf of a third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee calls or transmits to a station other than an Amateur Station without the Authority's written permission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee listened in on the frequency before transmitting, to ascertain that no interference is likely to be caused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 40(1) to (5): the Amateur Station licensee is meeting the regulation` MEANS
        `the messages are in plain language and relate solely to the licensee's experiments or personal affairs (not business affairs) or those of the person with whom the licensee is communicating`
    AND (NOT `the Amateur Station is used for transmitting news, advertisements, communications of a business or non-experimental character, messages for pecuniary reward or messages for or on behalf of a third party`)
    AND (NOT `the licensee calls or transmits to a station other than an Amateur Station without the Authority's written permission`)
    AND `the licensee listened in on the frequency before transmitting, to ascertain that no interference is likely to be caused`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:798 | Power of Authority to order transmission
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:799 | 41. The Authority may, in exceptional circumstances, by notice in
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:800 | writing, require the licensee to transmit any message by means of his
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:801 | licensed Amateur Station.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 41 (power of Authority to order transmission) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:798-801)
GIVEN `exceptional circumstances exist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 41: the Authority may by notice in writing require the licensee to transmit a message by means of the licensed Amateur Station` MEANS `exceptional circumstances exist`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:803 | Portable stations
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:804 | 42. The Authority may approve an Amateur Station as a portable
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:805 | or mobile station, subject to such conditions as the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:806 | impose.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:808 | Experimental Station Licence
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 42 (portable stations) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:803-808)
GIVEN `the Authority approves the Amateur Station as a portable or mobile station, subject to its conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 42: the Amateur Station is a portable or mobile station` MEANS `the Authority approves the Amateur Station as a portable or mobile station, subject to its conditions`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:810 | Experimental Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:811 | 43. The Authority may grant an Experimental Station Licence —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:813 | (a) to such educational institutions, training establishments or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:814 | qualified persons as the Authority may determine for the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:815 | purpose of conducting research and development activities,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:816 | experiments or demonstrations in radio-communication; or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:817 | (b) to licensed dealers in, or manufacturers or importers of,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:818 | radio-communication equipment for the purpose of testing,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:819 | demonstration or conducting research and development in
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:820 | radio-communication equipment.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 43 (Experimental Station Licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:810-820)
GIVEN `the applicant is an educational institution, training establishment or qualified person the Authority determines, for research and development, experiments or demonstrations in radio-communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a licensed dealer in, or manufacturer or importer of, radio-communication equipment, for testing, demonstration or research and development` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 43: the Authority may grant an Experimental Station Licence` MEANS
    `the applicant is an educational institution, training establishment or qualified person the Authority determines, for research and development, experiments or demonstrations in radio-communication` OR `the applicant is a licensed dealer in, or manufacturer or importer of, radio-communication equipment, for testing, demonstration or research and development`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:822 | Power limitations
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:823 | 44. The Authority may limit the maximum power of a station in
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:824 | respect of which an Experimental Station Licence has been issued,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:825 | having regard to the purpose for which the station has been
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:826 | authorised and the conditions under which it is to work.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:828 | Localised Radio-communication Station Licence
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 44 (power limitations) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:822-828)
GIVEN `the Authority has regard to the purpose for which the station has been authorised and the conditions under which it is to work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 44: the Authority may limit the maximum power of the Experimental Station` MEANS `the Authority has regard to the purpose for which the station has been authorised and the conditions under which it is to work`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:830 | Localised Radio-communication Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:831 | 45. The Authority may grant a Localised Radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:832 | Station Licence to approved applicants to use the following
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:833 | equipment:
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:834 | (a) remote control devices;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:835 | (b) local area paging devices;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:836 | (c) wireless microphones;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:837 | (d) transceivers (CB walkie talkies);
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:838 | (e) telemetry or alarm systems or both;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:839 | (f) wireless data or voice systems;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:840 | (g) cordless telephones; and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:841 | (h) any other radio-communication equipment as may be
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:842 | authorised by the Authority from time to time.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 45 (Localised Radio-communication Station Licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:830-842)
GIVEN equipment IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 45: the Authority may grant a Localised Radio-communication Station Licence to approved applicants to use the equipment` MEANS
    elem equipment (LIST "remote control devices", "local area paging devices", "wireless microphones", "transceivers (CB walkie talkies)", "telemetry or alarm systems or both", "wireless data or voice systems", "cordless telephones", "any other radio-communication equipment as may be authorised by the Authority from time to time")

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:844 | Sharing of frequencies
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:845 | 46.—(1) The frequencies allocated to any Localised
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:846 | Radio-communication Station may be shared by other users and the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:847 | Authority shall not be held responsible for any interference arising
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:848 | from such use.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:854 | (2) Licensees operating on shared frequencies shall accept any
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:855 | interference that may result from the legitimate operation of stations,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:856 | including the operation of industrial, scientific and medical (I.S.M.)
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:857 | equipment, functioning in the I.S.M. Band.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:859 | General Radio-communication Station Licence
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 46 (sharing of frequencies) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:844-859)
GIVEN `the licensee operates on a shared frequency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interference results from the legitimate operation of stations, including industrial, scientific and medical (I.S.M.) equipment functioning in the I.S.M. Band` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 46(2): the licensee must accept the interference` MEANS
    `the licensee operates on a shared frequency` AND `the interference results from the legitimate operation of stations, including industrial, scientific and medical (I.S.M.) equipment functioning in the I.S.M. Band`

GIVEN `the frequencies are allocated to a Localised Radio-communication Station` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 46(1): the frequencies may be shared by other users, and the Authority is not responsible for interference arising from such use` MEANS `the frequencies are allocated to a Localised Radio-communication Station`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:861 | General Radio-communication Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:862 | 47. The Authority may grant a General Radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:863 | Station Licence to approved applicants for the purpose of enabling
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:864 | them to transmit, receive or transmit and receive messages by means
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:865 | of radio-communication.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 47 (General Radio-communication Station Licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:861-865)
GIVEN `the applicant is approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 47: the Authority may grant a General Radio-communication Station Licence to enable the applicant to transmit, receive, or transmit and receive messages by radio-communication` MEANS `the applicant is approved`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:867 | Common based station and shared frequencies
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:868 | 48. The Authority may, in the interest of frequency spectrum
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:869 | economy or for any other reason, require a General
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:870 | Radio-communication Station licensee to work with a common base
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:871 | station operated or licensed by the Authority or to share a frequency
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:872 | with other stations, subject to any terms and conditions which the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:873 | Authority may impose.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 48 (common based station and shared frequencies) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:867-873)
GIVEN `the Authority considers it in the interest of frequency spectrum economy or for any other reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 48: the Authority may require a General Radio-communication Station licensee to work with a common base station or share a frequency, subject to its terms and conditions` MEANS `the Authority considers it in the interest of frequency spectrum economy or for any other reason`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:875 | Navigation or detection of objects
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:876 | 49. The Authority may grant a General Radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:877 | Station Licence to an approved applicant for the purpose of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:878 | navigating or detecting objects by means of radio-communication.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:880 | Satellite Communication Station Licence
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 49 (navigation or detection of objects) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:875-880)
GIVEN `the applicant is approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is navigating or detecting objects by means of radio-communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 49: the Authority may grant a General Radio-communication Station Licence` MEANS `the applicant is approved` AND `the purpose is navigating or detecting objects by means of radio-communication`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:882 | Satellite Communication Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:883 | 50. The Authority may grant the following classes of Satellite
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:884 | Communication Station Licence to enable the licensee to transmit,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:885 | receive or transmit and receive messages by means of satellite
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:886 | communication for such purposes as may be authorised by the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:887 | Authority:
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:888 | (a) Very Small Aperture Terminal (VSAT) Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:889 | (b) Tracking, Telemetry and Command (TT&C) Earth Station
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:890 | Licence; and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:891 | (c) Earth Station Licence.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 50 (Satellite Communication Station Licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:882-891)
GIVEN class IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 50: the Authority may grant the class of Satellite Communication Station Licence` MEANS
    class EQUALS "Very Small Aperture Terminal (VSAT) Licence" OR class EQUALS "Tracking, Telemetry and Command (TT&C) Earth Station Licence" OR class EQUALS "Earth Station Licence"

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:893 | Obligations of licensee
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:894 | 51.—(1) A Satellite Communication Station licensee shall seek the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:895 | approval of the Authority for access to any space segment and shall
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:896 | comply with the relevant rules, regulations and procedures imposed
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:897 | by the satellite operator for station access, booking and fees.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:898 | (2) Unless exempted by the Authority, the licensee shall at all
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:899 | times comply with the provisions of the International Telecommuni-
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:900 | cation Convention and all regulations and recommendations annexed
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:901 | thereto or made thereunder as are applicable to Singapore.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 51 (obligations of licensee) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:893-901)
GIVEN `the licensee sought the approval of the Authority for access to any space segment and complies with the rules, regulations and procedures of the satellite operator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority exempted the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee at all times complies with the International Telecommunication Convention and the regulations and recommendations applicable to Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 51: the Satellite Communication Station licensee is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    `the licensee sought the approval of the Authority for access to any space segment and complies with the rules, regulations and procedures of the satellite operator` AND (`the Authority exempted the licensee` OR `the licensee at all times complies with the International Telecommunication Convention and the regulations and recommendations applicable to Singapore`)

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:903 | Restrictions on frequencies, use, etc.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:904 | 52.—(1) A Satellite Communication Station licensee may only use
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:905 | or work within the frequencies or frequency bands approved by the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:906 | Authority for his use.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:907 | (2) Except with the written approval of the Authority, a Satellite
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:908 | Communication Station licensee shall not use any satellite communi-
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:909 | cation equipment in respect of which a Satellite Communication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:910 | Licence has been issued to provide telecommunication services to the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:911 | public.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:913 | Special Purpose Station Licence
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 52 (restrictions on frequencies, use, etc.) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:903-913)
GIVEN `the licensee uses or works only within the frequencies or frequency bands approved by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee uses satellite communication equipment to provide telecommunication services to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority approved it in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 52: the Satellite Communication Station licensee is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    `the licensee uses or works only within the frequencies or frequency bands approved by the Authority` AND ((NOT `the licensee uses satellite communication equipment to provide telecommunication services to the public`) OR `the Authority approved it in writing`)

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:915 | Special Purpose Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:916 | 53.—(1) The Authority may issue a Special Purpose Station
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:917 | Licence for the installation and operation of any special purpose
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:918 | station.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:919 | (2) For the purposes of this regulation, a ‘‘Special Purpose
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:920 | Station’’ is a station not otherwise defined in these Regulations which
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:921 | is established exclusively for such purpose and upon such terms and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:922 | conditions as the Authority may specify.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:924 | PART IIIA
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:925 | CLASS LICENCE
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 53 (Special Purpose Station Licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:915-925)
GIVEN `the station is not otherwise defined in the Regulations and is established exclusively for the purpose and on the terms and conditions the Authority specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 53: the Authority may issue a Special Purpose Station Licence for the installation and operation of the special purpose station` MEANS `the station is not otherwise defined in the Regulations and is established exclusively for the purpose and on the terms and conditions the Authority specifies`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:927 | Class licence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:928 | 53A.—(1) A person who possesses or uses a relevant
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:929 | radio-communication station shall be deemed to have been granted a
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:930 | class licence by the Authority for that purpose.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:933 | (2) A class licence shall be subject to the conditions specified in the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:934 | Fourth Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:935 | (3) Where a person has an existing licence for the possession or use
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:936 | of a relevant radio-communication station, that licence shall be
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:937 | revoked as from 1st April 1997 and he shall be deemed to have been
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:938 | granted a class licence.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:939 | (4) For the purposes of this regulation and the Fourth Schedule,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:940 | ‘‘relevant radio-communication station’’ means a radio-communica-
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:941 | tion station that is connected with any of the following telecommu-
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:942 | nication systems licensed under section 26 of the Act:
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:943 | (a) a public cellular mobile telephone system;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:944 | (b) a public radio paging system;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:945 | (c) a public data system;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:946 | (d) a public trunked radio system;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:947 | (e) a public satellite mobile telephone or data system,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:948 | and includes a radio-communication station that is capable of being
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:949 | used in connection with any of the telecommunication systems
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:950 | referred to in sub-paragraphs (a) to (e) but which is not in use and not
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:951 | so connected.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:953 | PART IV
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:954 | INTERFERENCE TO TELECOMMUNICATIONS
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 53A (class licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:927-954)
GIVEN `the person possesses or uses a relevant radio-communication station` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 53A(1): the person is deemed to have been granted a class licence by the Authority for that purpose` MEANS `the person possesses or uses a relevant radio-communication station`

GIVEN `the class licensee complies with the conditions specified in the Fourth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 53A(2): the class licence is subject to the conditions, and the class licensee is meeting them` MEANS `the class licensee complies with the conditions specified in the Fourth Schedule`

GIVEN `the person has an existing licence for the possession or use of a relevant radio-communication station` IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 53A(3): the existing licence is revoked, and the person is deemed to have been granted a class licence, as from 1 April 1997` MEANS
    `the person has an existing licence for the possession or use of a relevant radio-communication station` AND d AT LEAST (Date 1 4 1997)

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:956 | Inspection to determine cause of interference
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:957 | 54. An owner or user of electrical, electronic or radio-
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:958 | communication equipment causing or suspected of causing electrical
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:959 | or radiated interference or disturbance to telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:960 | equipment, stations, networks or systems belonging to or authorised
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:961 | or approved by the Authority shall permit an authorised officer to
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:962 | inspect his equipment in order to determine whether the interference
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:963 | is in fact caused by his equipment.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 54 (inspection to determine cause of interference) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:956-963)
GIVEN `the person is an owner or user of electrical, electronic or radio-communication equipment causing or suspected of causing electrical or radiated interference or disturbance to equipment, stations, networks or systems belonging to or authorised or approved by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person permits an authorised officer to inspect the equipment to determine whether the interference is in fact caused by it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 54: the owner or user is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    (NOT `the person is an owner or user of electrical, electronic or radio-communication equipment causing or suspected of causing electrical or radiated interference or disturbance to equipment, stations, networks or systems belonging to or authorised or approved by the Authority`) OR `the person permits an authorised officer to inspect the equipment to determine whether the interference is in fact caused by it`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:965 | Investigation by Authority upon request
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:966 | 55.—(1) The Authority may, where requested by any person to —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:967 | (a) investigate, for the second or subsequent time, the cause of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:968 | electrical or radiated interference or disturbance to telecom-
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:969 | munication equipment, stations, networks or systems; or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:971 | (b) measure and compute the field-strength of radiated electro-
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:972 | magnetic energy of any electrical, electronic or radio-
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:973 | communication equipment,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:974 | levy a fee of $100 per hour or part thereof for work done.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:975 | (2) Where the Authority undertakes to measure and compute the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:976 | field-strength of radiated electromagnetic energy under paragraph
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:977 | (1), the Authority shall determine the measuring device to be used,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:978 | the method by which and the conditions under which tests are to be
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:979 | conducted and the manner in which the field-strength from readings
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:980 | afforded by the measuring device is computed.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 55 (investigation by Authority upon request) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:965-980)
GIVEN `a person requests the Authority to investigate the cause of interference for the second or subsequent time, or to measure and compute field-strength` IS A BOOLEAN
      hours IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 55(1): the fee in dollars the Authority may levy for the work done (at $100 per hour or part thereof)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a person requests the Authority to investigate the cause of interference for the second or subsequent time, or to measure and compute field-strength` THEN JUST (100 TIMES hours)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:982 | Instructions to eliminate or reduce interference
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:983 | 56.—(1) Where the Authority determines that interference or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:984 | disturbance to telecommunication equipment, stations, networks or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:985 | systems is or may be caused by any particular electrical, electronic or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:986 | radio-communication equipment, the Authority may, by notice in
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:987 | writing, direct the owner or user of that electrical, electronic or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:988 | radio-communication equipment to do, at his own expense, any one
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:989 | or more of the following:
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:990 | (a) take suitable measures to eliminate or reduce the inter-
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:991 | ference or disturbance;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:992 | (b) remedy a fault in or the improper operation of the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:993 | equipment;
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:994 | (c) modify or alter the equipment; or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:995 | (d) disconnect the equipment.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:996 | (2) The Authority may require any action required to be taken
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:997 | under paragraph (1) to be effected within such period of time as the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:998 | Authority may determine having regard to the circumstances of each
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:999 | case.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1000 | (3) If the owner or user fails to comply with the directions issued
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1001 | by the Authority under paragraph (1) or (2), the Authority may, by
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1002 | notice in writing, prohibit the installation or use of that equipment
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1003 | unless and until such directions are complied with.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1004 | (4) In addition to any action the Authority may take under this
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1005 | regulation, the Authority may, where it considers it necessary —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1006 | (a) seal or remove the electrical, electronic or radio-
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1007 | communication equipment or any part thereof referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1008 | paragraph (1); and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1011 | (b) by notice in writing, direct any supplier of electricity to stop
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1012 | the supply of electricity to the owner or user of the electrical,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1013 | electronic or radio-communication equipment.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1015 | PART V
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1016 | MISCELLANEOUS
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 56 (instructions to eliminate or reduce interference) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:982-1016)
GIVEN `the Authority determines that interference or disturbance is or may be caused by particular equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 56(1): the Authority may by notice in writing direct the owner or user to eliminate or reduce the interference, remedy a fault, modify or alter the equipment, or disconnect it, at his own expense` MEANS `the Authority determines that interference or disturbance is or may be caused by particular equipment`

GIVEN `the owner or user fails to comply with the directions issued under paragraph (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 56(3): the Authority may by notice in writing prohibit the installation or use of the equipment until the directions are complied with` MEANS `the owner or user fails to comply with the directions issued under paragraph (1) or (2)`

GIVEN `the Authority considers it necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 56(4): the Authority may seal or remove the equipment, and direct a supplier of electricity to stop the supply` MEANS `the Authority considers it necessary`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1018 | Offence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1019 | 57. Any person who contravenes or fails to comply with any of the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1020 | provisions of these Regulations shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 57 (offence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:1018-1020)
GIVEN `the person contravenes or fails to comply with a provision of the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 57: the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS `the person contravenes or fails to comply with a provision of the Regulations`

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1022 | Composition of offences
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1023 | 58. An employee of the Authority specially authorised by name in
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1024 | that behalf by the Chief Executive may, in his discretion, compound
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1025 | any offence under these Regulations by collecting from the person
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1026 | reasonably suspected of committing the offence a sum not exceeding
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1027 | $1,000.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 58 (composition of offences) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:1022-1027)
GIVEN sum IS A NUMBER
      `the employee of the Authority is specially authorised by name by the Chief Executive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 58: the employee may compound the offence by collecting the sum from a person reasonably suspected of committing it` MEANS
    `the employee of the Authority is specially authorised by name by the Chief Executive` AND sum AT MOST 1000

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1029 | Radio-communications by members of the armed forces and other
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1030 | forces
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1031 | 59. No member of any armed forces, Singapore Civil Defence
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1032 | Force or police force shall use any station owned by him or by the said
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1033 | forces without a licence granted under these Regulations, unless such
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1034 | member uses the station in the course of his duties or in connection
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1035 | with a network used exclusively by the forces.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 59 (radio-communications by members of the armed forces and other forces) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:1029-1035)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the armed forces, the Singapore Civil Defence Force or a police force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses a station owned by him or by the forces without a licence under the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in the course of his duties or in connection with a network used exclusively by the forces` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 59: the member contravenes the regulation` MEANS
    `the person is a member of the armed forces, the Singapore Civil Defence Force or a police force` AND `the person uses a station owned by him or by the forces without a licence under the Regulations` AND (NOT `the use is in the course of his duties or in connection with a network used exclusively by the forces`)

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1037 | Waiver and exemption
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1038 | 60. The Minister or the Authority (subject to the directions of the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1039 | Minister) may waive any or all of the terms and conditions in any
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1040 | licence and any fee payable under these Regulations and may exempt
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1041 | any person from any or all of the provisions of these Regulations.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 60 (waiver and exemption) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:1037-1041)
GIVEN `the Minister or the Authority acts subject to the directions of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 60: the Minister or the Authority may waive any or all of the terms and conditions in any licence and any fee payable and exempt any person from any or all of the provisions` MEANS `the Minister or the Authority acts subject to the directions of the Minister`

