-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1183 | scanning devices) and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1184 | 2537.250 MHz
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1185 | Microwave
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1186 | Multipoint 2553.250 MHz
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1187 | Distribution Systems 2569.250 MHz
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1188 | (MMDS) Receivers 2601.250 MHz
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1189 | 2617.250 MHz
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1190 | 2633.250 MHz
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1191 | 2649.250 MHz
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1192 | 2665.250 MHz.
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) First Schedule (equipment for which no station licence is required for in-building or localised on-site operations) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:1043-1192)
-- The first band of item 4 prints "MHz 500 mW ERP" (a stray "MHz" before the limit); it is recorded here as "500 mW ERP".  Item 11 prints sub-items (a) to (f) under one pair of bands; the six are separate entries here, as in the N 1 Schedule that later carried the same list.
-- The item-numbered entries use the enumeration of the N 1 Schedule's equipment (sgta-nouns.l4), whose constructor for item 11(e) is `Remote Control Devices (e) TV Receivers or Radio Systems`: the later texts print "TV Receivers/ Radio Systems", this one prints "TV Receivers/ Radio Systems".
GIVETH A LIST OF `N 1 schedule item`
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) First Schedule items` MEANS
    LIST `CB Walkie Talkie Transceivers`
       , `Multi-channel Walkie Talkie Transceivers`
       , `Wireless Microphones`
       , `CB Band Radio Paging Systems`
       , `Induction Loop Communication Systems`
       , `VHF Radio Paging System`
       , `Radio Detection and Alarm Systems`
       , `Medical and Biological Telemetry Devices`
       , `Wireless Modem`
       , `Radio Telemetry Equipment`
       , `Remote Control Devices (a) Garage Door Openers`
       , `Remote Control Devices (b) Cameras`
       , `Remote Control Devices (c) Toys and Robots`
       , `Remote Control Devices (d) Battery-operated Cars and Boats`
       , `Remote Control Devices (e) TV Receivers or Radio Systems`
       , `Remote Control Devices (f) Other Miscellaneous Remote Control Devices`
       , `Cordless Telephones or Wireless PABX`
       , `Wireless LAN or Low Power Devices`
       , `Stand-alone GPS Receivers`
       , `Communication Receivers (excluding Scanning devices) and MMDS Receivers`

GIVEN item IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) First Schedule: the authorised frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` MEANS
    BRANCH IF item EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING
           IF item EQUALS 1 THEN JUST (LIST "26.96-27.28 MHz: 500 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 2 THEN JUST (LIST "477.000-477.250 MHz: 500 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 3 THEN JUST (LIST "0.51-1.60 MHz: 57 dB @ 3m", "40.66-40.70 MHz: 65 dB @ 10m", "88.00-108.00 MHz: 60 dB @ 10m", "180.000-200.000 MHz: 112 dB @ 10m", "487.000-507.000 MHz: 112 dB @ 10m")
           IF item EQUALS 4 THEN JUST (LIST "26.96-27.28 MHz: 500 mW ERP", "40.66-40.70 MHz: 500 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 5 THEN JUST (LIST "0.016-0.150 MHz: 100 dB @ 3m")
           IF item EQUALS 6 THEN JUST (LIST "151.125 MHz: 1000 mW ERP", "151.150 MHz: 1000 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 7 THEN JUST (LIST "0.016-0.150 MHz: 100 dB @ 3m", "26.96-27.28 MHz: 500 mW ERP", "146.350-146.500 MHz: 100 mW ERP", "240.150-240.300 MHz: 100 mW ERP", "300.000-300.300 MHz: 100 mW ERP", "314.700-315.000 MHz: 100 mW ERP", "444.400-444.800 MHz: 100 mW ERP", "10.50-10.55 GHz: 117dB @ 10m")
           IF item EQUALS 8 THEN JUST (LIST "40.500-41.000 MHz: 0.01 mW ERP", "454.000-454.500 MHz: 2 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 9 THEN JUST (LIST "72.080 MHz: 1000 mW ERP", "72.200 MHz: 1000 mW ERP", "72.400 MHz: 1000 mW ERP", "72.600 MHz: 1000 mW ERP", "158.275/162.875 MHz: 1000 mW ERP", "158.325/162.925 MHz: 1000 mW ERP", "453.7250/458.7250 MHz: 1000 mW ERP", "453.7375/458.7375 MHz: 1000 mW ERP", "453.7500/458.7500 MHz: 1000 mW ERP", "453.7625/458.7625 MHz: 1000 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 10 THEN JUST (LIST "26.96-27.28 MHz: 500 mW ERP", "29.700-30.000 MHz: 500 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 11 THEN JUST (LIST "26.96-27.28 MHz: 500 mW ERP", "40.66-40.70 MHz: 500 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 12 THEN JUST (LIST "1.605-1.800 MHz: 94dB @ 3m", "40.00-40.50 MHz: 57dB @ 3m", "46.50-47.00 MHz: 90dB @ 3m", "49.50-50.00 MHz: 90dB @ 3m", "864.10-868.10 MHz: 10 mW ERP", "1,880.00-1,918.10 MHz: 250 mW EIRP")
           IF item EQUALS 13 THEN JUST (LIST "433.79-434.79 MHz: 10 mW ERP", "864.10-868.60 MHz: 10 mW ERP", "819.00-823.00 MHz: 100 mW ERP", "1,880.00-1,930.00 MHz: 250 mW EIRP", "2,445.00-2,483.50 MHz*: 100 mW EIRP (* for in-building operations only)", "5,725.00-5,875.00 MHz: 100 mW EIRP", "18,820-18,870 MHz: 500 mW EIRP", "19,160-19,210 MHz: 500 mW EIRP", "24,000-24,250 MHz: 100 mW EIRP")
           IF item EQUALS 14 THEN JUST (LIST "1,575.420 MHz")
           IF item EQUALS 15 THEN JUST (LIST "2505.250 MHz", "2521.250 MHz", "2537.250 MHz", "2553.250 MHz", "2569.250 MHz", "2601.250 MHz", "2617.250 MHz", "2633.250 MHz", "2649.250 MHz", "2665.250 MHz")
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `the equipment is other low power equipment operating in a frequency band other than those listed for the same type of equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it meets the output power limits specified for the same type of equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Telecommunication Authority of Singapore approved both the output power limits and the frequency bands` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) First Schedule footnote: the other low power equipment is exempted from licensing` MEANS
        `the equipment is other low power equipment operating in a frequency band other than those listed for the same type of equipment`
    AND `it meets the output power limits specified for the same type of equipment`
    AND `the Telecommunication Authority of Singapore approved both the output power limits and the frequency bands`

GIVEN item IS AN `N 1 schedule item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) First Schedule: the item names the equipment` MEANS elem item (`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) First Schedule items`)

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1195 | SECOND SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1196 | Regulations 23 and 24
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1198 | PART I
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1200 | FEES FOR STATION/NETWORK LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1202 | First column Second column
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1203 | Types of licences Fee payable per annum
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1204 | 1. Ship Station $50
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1206 | 2. Aircraft Station $50
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1208 | 3. Amateur Station —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1209 | (a) General Class $50
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1210 | (b) Restricted Class $25
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1212 | 4. Experimental Station $50
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1214 | SECOND SCHEDULE — continued
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1216 | PART I — continued
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1218 | First column Second column
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1219 | Types of licences Fee payable per annum
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1220 | 5. Localised Radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1221 | Station —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1222 | (a) Remote Control Devices (aircraft (i) $25 (Personal use)
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1223 | models and cranes) (ii) $50 (Business use)
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1224 | (b) Local Area Paging Devices Base $50
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1225 | Station
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1226 | (c) Wireless Microphones (i) $25 (Personal use)
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1227 | (ii) $50 (Business use)
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1228 | (d) Transceivers (CB Walkie Talkies) (i) $25 (Personal use)
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1229 | (ii) $50 (Business use)
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1230 | (e) Telemetry and/or Alarm Systems $50
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1231 | (f) Wireless Data/Voice Systems (i) $50 for 50 stations or less
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1232 | (ii) $100 for more than 50
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1233 | stations
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1234 | 6. General Radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1235 | Station —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1236 | (a) Base/Fixed Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1237 | (b) Mobile Station $50
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1238 | (c) Fixed Link/Relay Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1239 | (d) Radiodetermination Station $50
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1240 | (e) Coast Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1241 | (f) Aeronautical Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1243 | 7. Satellite Communication Station —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1244 | (a) Very Small Aperture Terminal $100
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1245 | (VSAT)
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1246 | (b) Tracking, Telemetry and Command $100
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1247 | (TT & C) Earth Station
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1248 | (c) Ground Earth Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1249 | (d) Portable Satellite Communication $50
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1250 | Terminal
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1254 | SECOND SCHEDULE — continued
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1256 | PART I — continued
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1258 | First column Second column
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1259 | Types of licences Fee payable per annum
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1260 | 8. Localised Private Network —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1261 | (a) Portable/Mobile Station $100 per network
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1262 | (b) Base/Repeater Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1264 | 9. Wide-area Private Network —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1265 | (a) Portable/Mobile Station $500 per group of 50 stations
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1266 | or part thereof
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1267 | (b) Base/Repeater Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1269 | 10. Public Mobile Network —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1270 | (a) 300 Base Stations or less $100 per station
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1271 | (b) 301 to 500 Base Stations $80 per station for all stations
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1272 | (c) 501 to 700 Base Stations $60 per station for all stations
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1273 | (d) 701 Base Stations or more $40 per station for all stations.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1275 | PART II
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1277 | APPLICATION AND PROCESSING FEE
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1278 | FOR USE OF A FREQUENCY
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1280 | First column Second column
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1281 | Category Fee payable per frequency
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1282 | 1. Commonly Assigned Frequencies (for $100
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1283 | temporary or occasional use)
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1284 | 2. All Other Frequencies —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1285 | (a) Bandwidth of 25 kHz or less $290
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1286 | (b) Bandwidth of more than 25 kHz but $450
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1287 | less than 500 kHz
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1288 | (c) Bandwidth of 500 kHz or more but $1,350
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1289 | less than 1 MHz
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1290 | (d) Bandwidth of 1 MHz or more but $2,700
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1291 | less than 20 MHz
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1292 | (e) Bandwidth of 20 MHz or more $4,650
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1293 | 3. Satellite Downlink Frequencies $750 per band.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1295 | SECOND SCHEDULE — continued
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1297 | PART III
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1299 | ANNUAL FEES FOR USE OF FREQUENCY
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1301 | First column Second column
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1302 | Fee payable per frequency
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1303 | Radio Frequency Spectrum per annum
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1304 | 1. Frequencies for Networks and
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1305 | Systems —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1306 | (a) Exclusive Use
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1307 | (i) Bandwidth of less than 1 $300 per 25 kHz of occupied
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1308 | MHz bandwidth or part thereof
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1309 | (ii) Bandwidth of 1 MHz or $12,000 for the first MHz of
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1310 | more occupied bandwidth, and $300
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1311 | per subsequent MHz of occupied
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1312 | bandwidth or part thereof
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1313 | (b) Shared Use
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1314 | (i) Bandwidth of less than 300 $300 per 25 kHz of occupied
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1315 | kHz bandwidth or part thereof
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1316 | (ii) Bandwidth of 300 kHz or $3,500
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1317 | more but less than 20 MHz
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1318 | (iii) Bandwidth of 20 MHz or $6,200.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1319 | more
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1321 | 2. Satellite Downlink Frequencies $600 per band
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1323 | 3. Common Frequencies for In-building
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1324 | or On-site Wireless Systems —
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1325 | ISM Band Non ISM Band
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1326 | (a) Bandwidth of 20 MHz or less $ 50 $100
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1327 | (b) Bandwidth of more than 20 MHz $100 $200
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1328 | but not exceeding 50 MHz
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1329 | (c) Bandwidth of more than 50 MHz $150 $300
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1331 | 4. Block of Assigned Frequencies for $15.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1332 | Multi-channel Radio Communication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1333 | Networks and Systems
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) Second Schedule (fees) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:1195-1333)
GIVEN licence IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) Second Schedule Part I: the fee payable per annum for the type of licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF licence EQUALS "Ship Station" THEN JUST "$50"
           IF licence EQUALS "Aircraft Station" THEN JUST "$50"
           IF licence EQUALS "Amateur Station (a) General Class" THEN JUST "$50"
           IF licence EQUALS "Amateur Station (b) Restricted Class" THEN JUST "$25"
           IF licence EQUALS "Experimental Station" THEN JUST "$50"
           IF licence EQUALS "Localised Radio-communication Station (a) Remote Control Devices (aircraft models and cranes)" THEN JUST "(i) $25 (Personal use); (ii) $50 (Business use)"
           IF licence EQUALS "Localised Radio-communication Station (b) Local Area Paging Devices Base Station" THEN JUST "$50"
           IF licence EQUALS "Localised Radio-communication Station (c) Wireless Microphones" THEN JUST "(i) $25 (Personal use); (ii) $50 (Business use)"
           IF licence EQUALS "Localised Radio-communication Station (d) Transceivers (CB Walkie Talkies)" THEN JUST "(i) $25 (Personal use); (ii) $50 (Business use)"
           IF licence EQUALS "Localised Radio-communication Station (e) Telemetry and/or Alarm Systems" THEN JUST "$50"
           IF licence EQUALS "Localised Radio-communication Station (f) Wireless Data/Voice Systems" THEN JUST "(i) $50 for 50 stations or less; (ii) $100 for more than 50 stations"
           IF licence EQUALS "General Radio-communication Station (a) Base/Fixed Station" THEN JUST "$100"
           IF licence EQUALS "General Radio-communication Station (b) Mobile Station" THEN JUST "$50"
           IF licence EQUALS "General Radio-communication Station (c) Fixed Link/Relay Station" THEN JUST "$100"
           IF licence EQUALS "General Radio-communication Station (d) Radiodetermination Station" THEN JUST "$50"
           IF licence EQUALS "General Radio-communication Station (e) Coast Station" THEN JUST "$100"
           IF licence EQUALS "General Radio-communication Station (f) Aeronautical Station" THEN JUST "$100"
           IF licence EQUALS "Satellite Communication Station (a) Very Small Aperture Terminal (VSAT)" THEN JUST "$100"
           IF licence EQUALS "Satellite Communication Station (b) Tracking, Telemetry and Command (TT & C) Earth Station" THEN JUST "$100"
           IF licence EQUALS "Satellite Communication Station (c) Ground Earth Station" THEN JUST "$100"
           IF licence EQUALS "Satellite Communication Station (d) Portable Satellite Communication Terminal" THEN JUST "$50"
           IF licence EQUALS "Localised Private Network (a) Portable/Mobile Station" THEN JUST "$100 per network"
           IF licence EQUALS "Localised Private Network (b) Base/Repeater Station" THEN JUST "$100"
           IF licence EQUALS "Wide-area Private Network (a) Portable/Mobile Station" THEN JUST "$500 per group of 50 stations or part thereof"
           IF licence EQUALS "Wide-area Private Network (b) Base/Repeater Station" THEN JUST "$100"
           IF licence EQUALS "Public Mobile Network (a) 300 Base Stations or less" THEN JUST "$100 per station"
           IF licence EQUALS "Public Mobile Network (b) 301 to 500 Base Stations" THEN JUST "$80 per station for all stations"
           IF licence EQUALS "Public Mobile Network (c) 501 to 700 Base Stations" THEN JUST "$60 per station for all stations"
           IF licence EQUALS "Public Mobile Network (d) 701 Base Stations or more" THEN JUST "$40 per station for all stations"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN category IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) Second Schedule Part II: the application and processing fee payable per frequency` MEANS
    BRANCH IF category EQUALS "Commonly Assigned Frequencies (for temporary or occasional use)" THEN JUST "$100"
           IF category EQUALS "All Other Frequencies (a) Bandwidth of 25 kHz or less" THEN JUST "$290"
           IF category EQUALS "All Other Frequencies (b) Bandwidth of more than 25 kHz but less than 500 kHz" THEN JUST "$450"
           IF category EQUALS "All Other Frequencies (c) Bandwidth of 500 kHz or more but less than 1 MHz" THEN JUST "$1,350"
           IF category EQUALS "All Other Frequencies (d) Bandwidth of 1 MHz or more but less than 20 MHz" THEN JUST "$2,700"
           IF category EQUALS "All Other Frequencies (e) Bandwidth of 20 MHz or more" THEN JUST "$4,650"
           IF category EQUALS "Satellite Downlink Frequencies" THEN JUST "$750 per band"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN spectrum IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) Second Schedule Part III: the annual fee payable per frequency` MEANS
    BRANCH IF spectrum EQUALS "Frequencies for Networks and Systems (a) Exclusive Use (i) Bandwidth of less than 1 MHz" THEN JUST "$300 per 25 kHz of occupied bandwidth or part thereof"
           IF spectrum EQUALS "Frequencies for Networks and Systems (a) Exclusive Use (ii) Bandwidth of 1 MHz or more" THEN JUST "$12,000 for the first MHz of occupied bandwidth, and $300 per subsequent MHz of occupied bandwidth or part thereof"
           IF spectrum EQUALS "Frequencies for Networks and Systems (b) Shared Use (i) Bandwidth of less than 300 kHz" THEN JUST "$300 per 25 kHz of occupied bandwidth or part thereof"
           IF spectrum EQUALS "Frequencies for Networks and Systems (b) Shared Use (ii) Bandwidth of 300 kHz or more but less than 20 MHz" THEN JUST "$3,500"
           IF spectrum EQUALS "Frequencies for Networks and Systems (b) Shared Use (iii) Bandwidth of 20 MHz or more" THEN JUST "$6,200"
           IF spectrum EQUALS "Satellite Downlink Frequencies" THEN JUST "$600 per band"
           IF spectrum EQUALS "Common Frequencies for In-building or On-site Wireless Systems (a) Bandwidth of 20 MHz or less (ISM Band $50; Non ISM Band $100)" THEN JUST "ISM Band $50; Non ISM Band $100"
           IF spectrum EQUALS "Common Frequencies for In-building or On-site Wireless Systems (b) Bandwidth of more than 20 MHz but not exceeding 50 MHz" THEN JUST "ISM Band $100; Non ISM Band $200"
           IF spectrum EQUALS "Common Frequencies for In-building or On-site Wireless Systems (c) Bandwidth of more than 50 MHz" THEN JUST "ISM Band $150; Non ISM Band $300"
           IF spectrum EQUALS "Block of Assigned Frequencies for Multi-channel Radio Communication Networks and Systems" THEN JUST "$15"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1340 | THIRD SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1341 | Regulation 37 (2)
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1343 | RADIO AMATEUR EXAMINATION FEES
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1345 | First column Second column Third column
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1346 | Fees payable by full-time
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1347 | secondary, pre-university,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1348 | Institute of Technical
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1349 | Education, Singapore, and Fees payable by
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1350 | Type of examination tertiary students all other persons
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1351 | 1. Part I (Theory) $20 $40
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1353 | 2. Part II (Morse Sending $25 $50.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1354 | and Receiving)
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) Third Schedule (Radio Amateur Examination fees) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:1340-1354)
GIVEN `part of the examination` IS A STRING
      `the candidate is a full-time secondary, pre-university, Institute of Technical Education, Singapore, or tertiary student` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) Third Schedule: the fee in dollars payable to sit for the part of the Radio Amateur Examination` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `part of the examination` EQUALS "Part I (Theory)" THEN JUST (BRANCH IF `the candidate is a full-time secondary, pre-university, Institute of Technical Education, Singapore, or tertiary student` THEN 20 OTHERWISE 40)
           IF `part of the examination` EQUALS "Part II (Morse Sending and Receiving)" THEN JUST (BRANCH IF `the candidate is a full-time secondary, pre-university, Institute of Technical Education, Singapore, or tertiary student` THEN 25 OTHERWISE 50)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1357 | FOURTH SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1358 | Regulation 53A
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1360 | CONDITIONS OF CLASS LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1362 | 1. No fee is payable for a class licence.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1364 | 2. A class licensee shall comply with the technical specifications laid down
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1365 | from time to time by the Authority in relation to the relevant radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1366 | station.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1368 | 3. A class licensee shall ensure that the relevant radio-communication station
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1369 | is approved by the Authority before it is used for connection to any tele-
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1370 | communication system or equipment belonging to a public telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1371 | licensee, and that the relevant radio-communication station is not tampered with or
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1372 | modified in any manner after the approval of the Authority has been obtained.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1374 | 4. A class licensee shall ensure that the relevant radio-communication station
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1375 | is not used for any unlawful purpose.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1377 | 5. The Authority may cancel or suspend a class licence if it is satisfied that the
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1378 | class licensee is contravening, or has contravened and is likely again to contravene,
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1379 | any of these conditions or the provisions of the Act or any regulations made
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1380 | thereunder.
-- src:TA1999-RADIO99:1381 | [G.N. Nos. S 328/94; S 144/96; S 161/97; S 615/98; S 227/99]
@ref Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) Fourth Schedule (conditions of class licence) (src:TA1999-RADIO99:1357-1381)
GIVEN fee IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) Fourth Schedule item 1: the fee payable for a class licence is as stated` MEANS fee EQUALS 0

GIVEN `the class licensee complies with the technical specifications laid down by the Authority in relation to the relevant radio-communication station` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the class licensee ensures the station is approved by the Authority before it is used for connection to a telecommunication system or equipment belonging to a public telecommunication licensee, and is not tampered with or modified after approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the class licensee ensures the station is not used for any unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) Fourth Schedule items 2 to 4: the class licensee is meeting the conditions` MEANS
        `the class licensee complies with the technical specifications laid down by the Authority in relation to the relevant radio-communication station`
    AND `the class licensee ensures the station is approved by the Authority before it is used for connection to a telecommunication system or equipment belonging to a public telecommunication licensee, and is not tampered with or modified after approval`
    AND `the class licensee ensures the station is not used for any unlawful purpose`

GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied that the class licensee is contravening, or has contravened and is likely again to contravene, a condition or a provision of the Act or regulations made under it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) Fourth Schedule item 5: the Authority may cancel or suspend the class licence` MEANS `the Authority is satisfied that the class licensee is contravening, or has contravened and is likely again to contravene, a condition or a provision of the Act or regulations made under it`

